# print(read(holder));
# print("went on");
# A typed store in compiled code passes no entry check of the runtime.
# Where the unit itself does not show that the value is within the type that the slot is restricted to, the value is checked before the store.
# That happens in every build, and the failing side crashes with a named error.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeUnknownCallsReturnUndefined: Link assumes that the shell's `id` returns undefined.
# So an Other reaches a slot that is restricted to `Leaf | undefined` through a result, a variable and a slot of another object.
# Without the check each of the three cases prints 14 and continues. Nothing is inlined: in an inlined copy the walk sees the call itself, knows nothing about its result, and the store tests the value.
# In a user's build the first two cases report "what a field holds is". The third crashes one store earlier, at the entry check of the carrier's own slot.
# Where a run adds testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, the check at the place that the value is read from crashes first: "the result of a call is", "what a variable holds is".
# OPTIONS: testing=AssumeUnknownCallsReturnUndefined
# RUN(TRUE): run-in-shell mechanisms=-Inlining globalThis.which = 0;
# TRUE: went on
# RUN(RESULT): run-in-shell mechanisms=-Inlining globalThis.which = 1;
# RESULT: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# RESULT-NEXT: found object in
# RESULT-NOT: went on
# RESULT: crashed with
# RUN(VARIABLE): run-in-shell mechanisms=-Inlining globalThis.which = 2;
# VARIABLE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# VARIABLE-NEXT: found object in
# VARIABLE-NOT: went on
# VARIABLE: crashed with
# RUN(SLOT): run-in-shell mechanisms=-Inlining globalThis.which = 3;
# SLOT: bun: internal AOT error: object mutation check failed
# SLOT-NEXT: StoreOfOtherType on an {{*}}, but the compiler proved that this never happens
# SLOT-NOT: went on
# SLOT: crashed with

